Hello Make: team,

a workshop pitch that ends with something you can hold.

Take any downloaded handle with a knurled grip. In a mesh tool the knurl is a
carpet of hundreds of faces; making the grooves deeper means redrawing the
part.

In Solidon3D 0.5.0 the knurl is one feature in the object tree, with pitch,
cell width and depth. Change three numbers and it is reapplied — and because a
pattern on a cylinder is measured in the unrolled surface, the grooves are
equally deep all the way round and the pattern closes without a seam. Print
the original and the modified grip, and you have a direct comparison of grip
and surface finish.

The more interesting half for a maker audience is what the part is afterwards:
still an exact body. As of this release, primitives are built with real faces
and edges, and holes, slots, countersinks, bosses, beads, grooves and threads
stay exact through moving, duplicating, rotating and removing. STEP goes in and
comes back out cleanly, so the result can be carried into a CAD system rather
than arriving as triangles.

Two more things that suit a workshop piece:

* An existing thread gets its counterpart on the other part at the press of a
  button, in a table size and as a fit. The starting point may be an imported
  thread: Solidon measures pitch, starts, handedness and nominal diameter, and
  refuses when no table size matches instead of rounding.
* Dimensions are edited on the model itself — click a hole, type its distance
  to the edge, watch the preview.

I am happy to provide a review licence and the models used. If you would
rather use a file from your own archive, better still: that is exactly the case
the recognition was built for.

Solidon3D is a desktop application for Windows, macOS and Linux. One-time
purchase, no subscription, no account: after a single activation it runs fully
offline. Interface and manual are available in six languages, and there is a
demo.

I am happy to provide a review licence, print-resolution images or answers to
